WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.835 --> 00:00:02.969
A Pentagon report is

00:00:02.969 --> 00:00:04.637
detailing a dramatic increase

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:06.239
in UFO sightings.

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:09.042
More than 350 since 2021.

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:10.410
Many of them are explained

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:13.346
as being drones, birds or weather events.

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:14.981
But about half of them

00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:16.683
remain unexplained.

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:17.283
And the office

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:18.885
that tracks these sightings

00:00:18.885 --> 00:00:19.486
and restricted

00:00:19.486 --> 00:00:20.587
military airspace

00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:22.122
says that some, quote,

00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:24.591
require further analysis.

00:00:24.724 --> 00:00:26.693
That's an understatement.

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:27.894
CNN's space and defense

00:00:27.894 --> 00:00:28.728
correspondent Kristen

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:31.097
Fisher has the details.

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:31.965
Boris and Amara,

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:32.699
Capitol Hill

00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:34.601
has been waiting for this report

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:35.869
from the office of the Director

00:00:35.869 --> 00:00:37.871
of National Intelligence or the DNI.

00:00:38.071 --> 00:00:39.706
And what this report found

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:42.042
is that there have been more than 300

00:00:42.042 --> 00:00:43.443
new sightings

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:43.777
of what

00:00:43.777 --> 00:00:47.047
the government calls UAPS or unidentified

00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:47.981
aerial phenomena

00:00:47.981 --> 00:00:50.450
or more commonly called UFOs.

00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:52.185
Since the last time that the DOD

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:52.685
and I

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:53.420
put out a report

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.622
like this back in 20, 21.

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:56.756
Back then,

00:00:56.756 --> 00:00:59.959
the odd and I could not explain 144

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:03.263
sightings of UAPs this time.

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:07.500
Now they can't explain 171 of them

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.002
in one part of the report

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:11.371
that really stands out is this one.

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:12.138
It says that

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:14.941
some of these uncharacterized UAPs

00:01:15.208 --> 00:01:16.876
appear to have demonstrated

00:01:16.876 --> 00:01:18.978
unusual flight characteristics

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:20.747
or performance capabilities

00:01:20.747 --> 00:01:22.749
and require further analysis.

00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:25.885
So is it advanced U.S.

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:26.619
technology,

00:01:26.619 --> 00:01:28.922
is it advanced technology from

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:30.190
a foreign adversary

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:32.258
like perhaps China or Russia,

00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:33.793
or is it

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:35.695
extraterrestrial in origin

00:01:35.695 --> 00:01:37.363
or something else entirely?

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:38.598
We just don't know.

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:39.332
And the U.S.

00:01:39.332 --> 00:01:40.333
government

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:42.402
says that it doesn't know either,

00:01:42.402 --> 00:01:44.571
or at least it will not say so

00:01:45.038 --> 00:01:48.241
publicly in this unclassified report.

00:01:48.842 --> 00:01:51.211
But they did give some explanations for

00:01:51.211 --> 00:01:53.880
about 163 of the sightings

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:55.715
that have been detailed in this report.

00:01:55.715 --> 00:01:57.750
And here's how they explained those

00:01:58.051 --> 00:01:59.853
The vast majority

00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:03.356
are either balloons or balloon entities.

00:02:03.823 --> 00:02:05.558
A handful were drones.

00:02:05.558 --> 00:02:07.927
Another handful were what they called

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:11.030
airborne clutter, things like birds,

00:02:11.231 --> 00:02:12.665
weather events

00:02:12.665 --> 00:02:15.168
or airborne debris, like plastic bags.

00:02:15.201 --> 00:02:16.503
So the bottom line

00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:18.204
here, members of Congress say

00:02:18.204 --> 00:02:19.172
that this is a

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:20.740
step in the right direction

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:22.709
to reducing the stigma

00:02:22.709 --> 00:02:24.777
associated with reporting

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:26.312
sightings of UAPS.

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:28.481
It's also a step in the right direction

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:30.183
to enhancing national security,

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:31.718
because remember,

00:02:31.718 --> 00:02:33.853
a lot of these sightings happen

00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:37.157
right around military bases or assets but

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:39.692
while it's a step in the right direction,

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:40.560
members of Congress

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:41.995
say the Pentagon,

00:02:41.995 --> 00:02:42.862
the Office of the director

00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:44.097
of National Intelligence,

00:02:44.097 --> 00:02:45.632
still have a long way

00:02:45.632 --> 00:02:47.100
to go to giving them

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.935
the answers that they ultimately want.

